L32_1 = [[
Merlin had been looking after the Stump to provide against a prophecy.
The villagers of the Stump looked up to Merlin, possessing thousands of years of knowledge and history, as their teacher and leader, and she dutifully obliged, imparting her knowledge to them.
Merlin, in particular, valued devoted love and taught it herself to the children. Hence the Stump's strict rules against adultery.
Merlin maintained a large vineyard where she made her own wine as a hobby. Her love for alcohol led her to always accompany any celebration with wine and spirits, even holding a festival at the Stump on wedding days with all the alcohol she had provided.]]
