L8_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_GRAFFITI"
L9_1 = [[
Rachel Dodds adds color and vitality to the bleak streets of the 6th refugee district.
Wherever she goes, she leaves beautiful graffiti on the walls she passes by. Her drawing skills are well-known among the neighborhood watch of the refugee district as well as the dangerous gangsters.
She still hasn't gotten over the recent incident that she experienced, but that doesn't seem to have any impact on her artistic impulse. She happily moves around with her employer plus friend, showing off her pieces.]]
L7_1[1] = L8_1
L7_1[2] = L9_1
L8_1 = {}
L9_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_HORIZON_M_LOAN"
L10_1 = [[
Horizon is a fearless defender who protects herself with persistent barrier generation and immunity effects while mercilessly knocking her enemies out of the way. 
She is a debt collector of the infamously cruel Horizon Finance. Despite the high interest rates and notoriety, however, her company is always struggling to stay in the black. Most of the profits end up going to pay for the collateral damage caused during collections. That's exacerbated by the fact that many of her debtors refuse to pay up until the little girl they scoffed at takes more direct action. 
Everyone around her can tell Horizon's not cut out for the job, but she doesn't seem to feel the need to make any improvements. If anything, she seems more interested in observing the people she meets during her collections, rather than the collection itself. 
Her victims insist Horizon just enjoys showing off her power and watching the response, but it remains to be seen if she has an ulterior motive.]]
L8_1[1] = L9_1
L8_1[2] = L10_1
L9_1 = {}
L10_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_HARMONY_C_VIOLIN"
L11_1 = [[
Shena is a close-range sniper who generates musical notes proportional to her CRIT rate and inflicts AoE damage.
Although she is the powerful head of Jehuty Biotech's security, she rarely shows herself in public. Most witnesses say she made quite the presence with her impromptu performance for VIP guests.
The Elysium Philharmonic she mentioned was a key antagonist of the Old Administration up till the Administration Failure, when it lost its supreme leader thanks to the actions of the old Divisions, still active at the time.
During the Elysium Philharmonic's heyday, Shena served the role of performing in the final act of their vicious symphonies. No one can tell if her reappearance indicates the resurgence of her organization, or if she's merely a straggler who's left behind in the real world.]]
L9_1[1] = L10_1
L9_1[2] = L11_1
L10_1 = {}
L11_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_FUTURE_MA_LOAN"
L12_1 = [[
Paraphrased from an excerpt in Dr. Ember's journal.
This combat mode allows Horizon to play the role of airborne striker, inflicting damage proportional to the target's HP.
Based on credible analysis, Cold Case number 137 was likely designed as an escort vehicle capable of dimensional jumps and interstellar navigation. Armaments required for engagement are procured via a platform called the Simurgh Silhouette. The barrier stasis field generated in non-combat mode is likely a means of protecting the vehicle during navigation.
This research has yielded tremendous gains in our own progress of android technology. However, as the entire research team has concurred that this frame is at risk of being misappropriated for use as a strategic weapon, we've decided to classify it as unusable and seal it away. 
I just hope it'll be put to much better use than my mind imagines.]]
L10_1[1] = L11_1
L10_1[2] = L12_1
L11_1 = {}
L12_1 = "SI_UNIT_SKILL_DESC_HORIZON_M_LOAN_SKILL_LV1"
L13_1 = "Tracks down the debtor and inflicts AoE damage, targeting the caster for 6 seconds. Ignores cooldown and casts skill for targets beyond 600 reach. When in enhanced state, damage is increased by 10% and Airborne becomes more powerful."
L11_1[1] = L12_1
L11_1[2] = L13_1
L12_1 = {}
