L14_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_GUILTY_S_MILLIA"
L15_1 = [[
Millia Rage is a ranger whose ability to attack continuously is especially effective against defenders with damage restriction. She also generates shock waves, pushing away nearby enemies.

A former member of the Assassin's Guild, she now leads the world's biggest intelligence agency. Her hair, imbued with the forbidden spell, Angra, can assume different shapes and solidity.
She's quiet and cold, but doesn't always make her decisions based on cost and benefit. With her kindness and compassion, she's featured as a training coach in the simulation.]]
L13_1[1] = L14_1
L13_1[2] = L15_1
L14_1 = {}
L15_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_GUILTY_S_MAY"
L16_1 = [[
May is a supporter who maximizes nearby allies' survivability through her decent HP and supportive abilities.
She was a war orphan who later became a member of the Jellyfish Pirates. Her small, dainty appearances belie her superhuman strength, which enables her to swing an anchor as if it weighs nothing. She can also summon aquatic animals with her magic skills. She believes in acting before thinking too deeply, and her friends, the Jellyfish Pirates, often get dragged along with her impulsive behavior.]]
L14_1[1] = L15_1
L14_1[2] = L16_1
L15_1 = {}
L16_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_GUILTY_M_INO"
L17_1 = [[
I-NO is a sniper delivering AoE attacks from a distance. She can blow away oncoming enemies to protect herself, and she's strong against flying units.
Her tendency to approach someone as if talking to an old friend and her interest in others can make I-NO seem personable at first glance. But she is not able to work with anyone and sees all others as lesser beings worthy of ridicule. Also, she instinctively reveals her violent temper to someone she finds hostile. Even though she's on the simulation list, she's not an ideal choice for team play because of her penchant to manipulate and torment others. Her real identity is a Magical Foci, a pseudo-lifeform created by the people's desire for a brighter tomorrow during the Crusades. This side of her has been reflected in the simulated Counter/Mech.]]
L15_1[1] = L16_1
L15_1[2] = L17_1
L16_1 = {}
L17_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_GUILTY_C_SOL"
L18_1 = [[
  Sol Badguy is a defender who can temporarily enhance himself and incapacitate surrounding enemies, depending on the number of attacks he delivers.

He claims to be a bounty hunter himself, but his primary target is to eliminate Gears, the bionic weapons scattered everywhere in the world. The way he fights, destroying his enemies with brute force instead of technique, is possible because he was restructured into a Gear himself.
 This simulated version of him seems just as brusque and aloof as his original. Still, he has to have a humane side that's been formed during his hitherto turbulent life.]]
L16_1[1] = L17_1
L16_1[2] = L18_1
L17_1 = {}
L18_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_GUILTY_C_RAMLETHAL"
L19_1 = [[
Ramlethal Valentine is a striker specializing in powerful close-range combo attacks.
She is a life form created in the image of humanity. The Valentines were tasked to destroy humanity and she also used to carry out her orders mechanically before she met someone and learned what it felt like to have emotions. She's been fighting on humanity's side since then.
Ramlethal, whose worldview is as innocent as a child's, would blend right in with socially awkward employees.]]
L17_1[1] = L18_1
L17_1[2] = L19_1
