L27_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_FALLEN_ROSARIA"
L28_1 = [[
 Rosaria le Friede is an all-around ranged attacker, delivering powerful AoE attacks from the air.

The owner of the Fallen Hawk Private Eye famous for its ability to find the missing, she's been seen by many of her clients treating her employees like her servants. According to her, she's only being gracious to lesser beings who wouldn't have known their purpose in life if it weren't for her.
She enjoys observing mankind's self-destructive and irrational behavior, and loves watching daytime soap operas. She's especially an avid fan of The Bridge of Seduction Season 6, widely popular for its immoral and controversial story.
Sometimes she accompanies her employees on their investigations, and whenever she does, mysterious cases of local destruction occur.]]
L26_1[1] = L27_1
L26_1[2] = L28_1
L27_1 = {}
L28_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_JAPAN_RYOHEI"
L29_1 = [[
 Nayuka Minato is a ranged attacker who inflicts deadly AoE damage from a safe distance.

His family, Nayuka, is at the bottom of the ladder of the Family Alliance led by Nanahara Family and is one of the very collateral family.
Because of this, Minato used to enjoy a peaceful life, away from the eventful circle of the Family Alliance. But then he awakened as a Counter because of an old watch he received from his grandfather, his life hasn't been the same.
Minato, instead of feeling responsibility for his newfound power, just wants to be a teenager like everyone else his age, going to school and working part-time.
Currently, the Family Alliance is in the process of electing its new leader and focusing on rebuilding itself, so it can maintain the seal. It will want to recruit this boy who has the blood of the Nanaharas in him, but whether or not he joins depends on him.]]
L27_1[1] = L28_1
L27_1[2] = L29_1
L28_1 = {}
L29_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_CA_ADMIN_LEE_SUYEON"
L30_1 = [[
 Lee Sooyeon has returned to the battlefield, armed with new gear! She's a powerful ranged attacker who sweeps enemies aside as she enters battle from the air, singlehandedly securing air supremacy.

She has been serving as the vice president of the Coffin Company, during which her career as a Grade S Counter became all but a memory. However, she recently made a secret comeback and proved she hasn't gotten rusty by renewing her old performance record with flying colors.
She's still the same miser with a cold, businesslike attitude, but at least now when she's in battle, she makes everyone forget that and remember why she's the ace of the company.
She takes pride in her fighting ability, but for some reason doesn't like to talk about her old fighting style.]]
L28_1[1] = L29_1
L28_1[2] = L30_1
L29_1 = {}
L30_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_SIXWING_LEE_JISOO"
L31_1 = [[
 Lee Jisoo is a melee supporter specializing in various curses, including Recovery reduction.

A member of an organization called Six Wings, she's often seen escorting her leader, Na Yubin, unlike the other members who rarely reveal themselves in public.
She's a dangerous person who has penetrated the Administration's security several times, with only her sword. Her Counter abilities are powerful curses, which she uses through her swordsmanship to subdue her enemies.
She's currently working undercover at a government office, but she has a bad reputation among her colleagues because she is always messing up at work. It is suspected that she, who must be a talented person, is pretending to be clumsy in order to avoid suspicion. What other reason could there be?]]
L29_1[1] = L30_1
L29_1[2] = L31_1
L30_1 = {}
L31_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_FALLEN_DOMA"
L32_1 = [[
 Frederick Doma is a ranged attacker who incapacitates his enemies and kills them slowly.

A suspicious receptionist at a suspicious detective agency, he's good at cajoling potential clients with his gentlemanly manner and eloquence. It's unfortunate that he doesn't know his extravagant appearances and peculiar manner of speech make his customers feel uncomfortable.
His mean, villainous appearance belies his reputation in the industry as a fair fighter. His enemies may feel differently about that because of his tendency to play games with them, even if he thinks that's fair.]]
L30_1[1] = L31_1
L30_1[2] = L32_1
L31_1 = {}
L32_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_REPLACER_CA_QUEEN"
L33_1 = [[
  The Replacer Queen is a sniper that controls enemies with Debuffs and continuously enhances herself through AoE attacks.

 Currently leading her organization in the King's place, she's considered as dangerous as a Category 4 C.O. Since she's been so diligent about eliminating spies in her organization, not much information has been released to the outside.
 But according to what's available to us, she's a fervent supporter of the King, but doesn't seem to be interested in his ideals.]]
L31_1[1] = L32_1
L31_1[2] = L33_1
L32_1 = {}
L33_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_REPLACER_C_KNIGHT"
L34_1 = [[
  The Replacer Knight is an offensive defender rushing anywhere on the field to destroy the enemy's formation.

 An international criminal wanted in multiple countries, she's notorious for her penchant for complete annihilation. Her violence, combined with her extreme elitism, also has made her unpopular among her men. 
 Based on the leaked research data, the Replacer Syndicate researchers purposefully instilled aggressiveness and elitism in their test subjects through forceful training and vicious competition. Please keep this in mind in case you come across her.]]
L32_1[1] = L33_1
L32_1[2] = L34_1
L33_1 = {}
L34_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_REPLACER_CA_KING"
L35_1 = [[
  The Replacer King is a defender capable of summoning multiple soldiers and delivering unlimited AoE attacks in certain situations.

 He's also the founder of the Replacer Syndicate, whose core members are fervent supporters of his ideals. Turncoats claim that the rest of the organization looks up to him as if he's a pioneer. 
 Despite vigorous attempts by various intelligence agencies, he's managed to keep his identity secret. Some people suspect he may have worked for an intelligence agency or an illegal military regiment that ran covert ops.]]
L33_1[1] = L34_1
L33_1[2] = L35_1
L34_1 = {}
L35_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_REPLACER_C_BISHOP"
L36_1 = [[
  The Replacer Bishop is a striker that can move stealthily across the field, without drawing attention from enemies.

 After the Replacer Syndicate researchers discovered the physical regenerative properties of the Replacer Factor, there has been an influx of people into this criminal organization who were diagnosed with permanent disabilities, and wanted a new life through the Replacer Factor. According to internal information, this Replacer Bishop is believed to be one of them.
 There are unconfirmed reports that she was gravely injured during a Corruption disaster, and is now fitted with gear to support her damaged body, which heavily relies on the Factor.
 She's an officer of the Syndicate, but because she's not as actively engaged in field operations as the others, most intelligence agencies believe that she's a specialist only dealing with specific missions.]]
L34_1[1] = L35_1
L34_1[2] = L36_1
L35_1 = {}
L36_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_CORRUPTED_C_SHADOW"
L37_1 = [[
  Spira is a Demon-type C.O. and a striker that rushes into enemy territory and attacks the rear line when her HP is low.

 Suspected to have transmuted into a Shadow just recently, she shows a strong desire to go back to reality, and the visible damage in her joints must have been from her body's resistance to the transmutation.
 Because she's been often seen with Ministra the Named Demon, it's believed that Spira was made a C.O. to be her watchdog.]]
L35_1[1] = L36_1
L35_1[2] = L37_1
L36_1 = {}
L37_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_PUPPET_C_BLIND"
L38_1 = [[
  Serapel is a defender that takes damage for allies around her.
 The Original Puppet, Serapel is believed to have been modeled after a woman in a fairy tale that goes...
 "Once upon a time, there lived a woman who was more beautiful than anyone under the sky. Everyone loved her, and she became so spoiled that nothing could satisfy her.
 Her desperate admirers committed all kinds of atrocities to please her, and eventually, she was punished for that by an angry mob. Just before her death, she felt thrilled for the first time in her life, through the pain and hatred that she'd never known before."]]
L36_1[1] = L37_1
L36_1[2] = L38_1
L37_1 = {}
L38_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_ALT_CA_SEO_YOON"
L39_1 = [[
  Seo Yoon has awakened her Altergressive power!
A ranger specializing in telekinetically controlling firearms and her spear Misteltein, she distinguished herself during the battle with the Replacers, and received an official license to run a squad, which used to operate illegally in the Underground.
 A lot of Underground Counters are jealous of her success, and it's a mystery among them why such an independent and successful individual would insist on staying with a small TASKFORCE company that doesn't seem to offer much.]]
L37_1[1] = L38_1
L37_1[2] = L39_1
L38_1 = {}
L39_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_SCAVENGER_S_HAMMER"
L40_1 = [[
  Overflow is a charger-type defender capable of resisting Knockback and pressing on through enemies.

 As the combatants of the Scavengers' penetration unit, Picador, Overflows take the lead and open up a path for the others once their looting target is decided. Because things worth stealing are always protected with great care. Their hammer, a non-firearm weapon that can hardly be seen anymore, works synergistically with their power suit, easily crushing through even the most reliable security system. Of course, people and weapons are no exceptions if they stood in its way.]]
L38_1[1] = L39_1
L38_1[2] = L40_1
L39_1 = {}
L40_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_CORRUPTED_CA_MINISTRA"
L41_1 = "  Ministra, a Demon-Type C.O., is a ranger who specializes in weakening the enemy through AoE debuffs. The objects she makes by reassembling her dead enemies spread fear and hopelessness.\n\n The other Shadows—or Sisters—she has created while wandering the Counterside all have a similar appearance to Spira, which implies the strong bond that once existed between them. She has sadistic tendencies and enjoys watching her prey wither away in isolation, leaving her victims with no prospect but a horrible death. Due to this, she has been categorized as \"extremely dangerous\" by the Administration."
L39_1[1] = L40_1
L39_1[2] = L41_1
L40_1 = {}
L41_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_SCHOOL_C_PENCIL"
L42_1 = "  Mika★Star is a supporter who uses marvelous magic tricks to harass and weaken enemies.\n\n Aspiring to be the greatest magician of the century, she represents the Academy's Counters who support noncombatism. She insists that everyone's dreams must be respected, and not all Counters need to focus on physical fighting skills. This must be why the Student President, who believes in harmony, has selected her for the Student Council.\n And just because she believes in noncombatism, it doesn't mean she's weak. Her magic, which she's been painstakingly practiced to present bold, exciting magic shows, becomes lethal off the stage."
L40_1[1] = L41_1
L40_1[2] = L42_1
L41_1 = {}
L42_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_SCAVENGER_C_COLLECT"
L43_1 = [[
  Machine Collector is a supporter commanding parasites to enhance allies, remove enemy buffs, and create additional effects for Mechs.

 She's the most infamous pirate on the Dark Network and a more threatening enemy to the companies that develop armored weapons than their competitors. With a simple flick of her fingers, she can instantly set her parasites on their machines, divesting them of control.
 As her name suggests, she collects machines. She also enjoys putting them to the test, which is the reason things in her collection usually don't last long. Unless she finds some machines that can endure her cruel treatment, her thirst as a collector won't be quenched.]]
L41_1[1] = L42_1
L41_1[2] = L43_1
L42_1 = {}
L43_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_KNIGHT_C_HOLY"
L44_1 = [[
  Lucrecia is an air ranger who can make her allies immortal with her blessings while releasing unholy energy at her enemies.

 A vital member of the Knights of Redemption, she fervently follows the figure named the Savior. She's often referred to as the Saintess because of the power she wields, known as the Blessings.

 But her concept of blessings and mercy is alarmingly different from their conventional meanings. There's only one form of redemption she wants, and all the sacrifices that may be created during the process of achieving this redemption are what she thinks of as blessings and mercy. She dreams of dangerous things and has the power to realize them. Interaction with her can be a bit too risky.]]
L42_1[1] = L43_1
L42_1[2] = L44_1
L43_1 = {}
L44_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_ETC_S_DOCTOR"
L45_1 = [[
  Lone Lee the villainess is a supporter capable of various debuffs, such as CRIT DMG Decrease.

 In the past, she was just a gloomy scientist well-versed in the Counterside effect. Unrequited love changed all that, making her hate all couples in the world.
 She joined the Administration's affiliated laboratory to study C.O. while plotting to destroy her enemies. Her plans went awry at a critical moment, and she was sent to prison.
 Now, she's successfully escaped, and no one knows what she's up to. What's clear is that she now works for someone and is no longer interested in destroying innocent couples.]]
L43_1[1] = L44_1
L43_1[2] = L45_1
L44_1 = {}
L45_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_PUPPET_C_WHIP"
L46_1 = [[
  Harab is a supporter who grows stronger the longer she attacks. She confuses the enemy's summoned units into attacking their own.

 Her Cronenworth Puppet Troupe is famous for its realistic puppet shows. Some of its fans are so fascinated by the performance that they believe they see the puppets actually shedding tears.
 Since the War, Harab Cronenworth has been traveling around the world, showcasing her incredible performance for free wherever she goes. When asked why she's doing this, she says she's looking for a puppet that's important to her. Lately, something about her has changed, which is the consensus among those who watched her recent performance.]]
L44_1[1] = L45_1
L44_1[2] = L46_1
L45_1 = {}
L46_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_SCAVENGER_S_CUTLASS"
L47_1 = [[
  Glitch is a striker that enters battle in Stealth mode.

 As the combatants of the Scavengers' looting unit, Peneo, they loot for a living like the others of their organization. Outside combat, they're engineers who spend their time maintaining machines and immersing themselves in technologies available on the Counterside. They work at a research lab where human augmentation is common and is always filled with inert gases and screams.
 Thanks to their unethical research environment and valuable Artifacts from the Counterside, they own technology that can compete with any TASKFORCE companies', its instability and twisted nature notwithstanding.]]
L45_1[1] = L46_1
L45_1[2] = L47_1
L46_1 = {}
L47_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_HORIZON_C_SCYTHE"
L48_1 = [[
  Dash is a sniper who shoots sharp winds at distant enemies, decreasing their DEF. Her scythe is made to agitate the air into a strong wind when swung.

 Dash is an intern at Horizon Finance, charged with mortgage interest collection. She's working off her parents' debt. Rita thinks she's a dratted broad who does nothing but causing trouble. The company's CEO, Horizon, thinks she's a mood maker who brightens up the workplace.]]
L46_1[1] = L47_1
L46_1[2] = L48_1
L47_1 = {}
L48_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_ACADEMY_S_HANDGUN"
L49_1 = [[
  Brownie Moore is a supporter who removes debuffs from ally Soldiers and temporarily reduces enemy damage on them.

 She was originally an adventurer who explored the ruins in the Counterside. She once hosted a popular documentary series, Man vs. Dive, but the show drew a lot of criticism that it portrayed the Counterside as a romantic vacation spot.
 Tired of constant criticism, she took up the job offer from the Student President and became a teacher at the Academy. Although it's a daily occurrence for her to cancel her classes and disappear, there isn't a single student who dislikes her because she always comes back with exciting adventure stories.]]
L47_1[1] = L48_1
L47_1[2] = L49_1
L48_1 = {}
L49_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_SIXWING_AMY"
L50_1 = [[
  Amy Firstwing is a sniper who uses strings to cut through enemies and control those that have survived.

 The strange way she dresses and behaves points at something very specific, but no one knows what. More accurately, anyone who tried to look into her past has disappeared without a trace. According to witness testimonies, she's careless, impatient, crass, and antisocial.
 But her actual record shows she's a meticulous specialist who leaves no loose ends. So, which one is the real her?]]
L48_1[1] = L49_1
L48_1[2] = L50_1
