L2_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_JAPAN_SETSUNA"
L3_1 = [[
 Nanahara Chinatsu, the young leader of the Family Alliance, is a supporter whose healing wind recovers allies and weakens enemies.

When the former Family leader suddenly fell ill and passed away, the Alliance unanimously elected Chinatsu as its new leader because she awakened the ability to hear the voice of wind just like the founder of her Family, who used his mystical power to foretell the future and read people's minds, bringing wealth and power to his family.
She hasn't fully mastered her power yet, but already people in and out of her Family are trying to take advantage of her. Chinatsu hasn't let them interfere with her running her Family or her dedication to her Family's tradition of fighting the Counterside.
]]
L1_1[1] = L2_1
L1_1[2] = L3_1
L2_1 = {}
L3_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_JAPAN_ZENJIROU"
L4_1 = [[
 Ogami Masaki is a defender who uses the dark flames that run through his veins.

His dark flames inflict powerful AoE damage while distracting enemies with their unique coloring.
He made up his surname, Ogami, as a reminder to himself of his ambition to control the Family Alliance from the shadows one day.
He's the leader of the well-known secret organization, Ogami's Shadow Group. He's also its only member since its establishment. His daily routine as a member of the Shadow Group includes practicing sinister laughter, brooding while sitting alone in the dark, and feigning knowledge that he doesn't have.
Currently, Masaki is looking for new members for his group. Most people in the Family Alliance treat him like an outcast, but given his ability as a Counter, he could be an important factor that could tip the scales of the Alliance's leader election. ]]
L2_1[1] = L3_1
L2_1[2] = L4_1
L3_1 = {}
L4_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_LENA"
L5_1 = [[
  Lena is an excellent student who graduated from the Operator Training Institute with the highest honors. Because she accomplished this so quickly, being determined to become a great Operator, her professors use her as an example to inspire their students during their first class at the Institute.
 Lena quit studying to become a governmental employee and became an Operator because she idolized Frederica, the heroine of the popular soap opera, the Bridge of Seduction. Unlike her idol, however, Lena still loves drinking beer.]]
L3_1[1] = L4_1
L3_1[2] = L5_1
L4_1 = {}
L5_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_ACADEMY_C_TWINTAIL"
L6_1 = "Naielle Bluesteel is a striker whose cheeky behavior stimulates aggression in allies. She is an elite who has never missed the top grade in the Academy's combat evaluation. She was notorious for looking down on inferior students, posing as a team leader among her childhood friends. However, she began to show anxiety after the appearance of a stronger rival, and her way of speaking changed strangely after a certain incident. Her attitude of disrespecting others still remains unchanged, but she now proudly calls herself \"garbage.\" With all the rumors put together, she is presumed to have been influenced by some kind of autosuggestion. According to an expert at the Student Council, it is very rare that a person gets hypnotized as easily as her."
L4_1[1] = L5_1
L4_1[2] = L6_1
L5_1 = {}
L6_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ADMIN_ARTILLERY"
L7_1 = [[
 (This text was restored by a Class 1 Administrator.)
Lyudmila uses naval artillery to bombard enemies from all sides and fill in fallen allies. Her telekinesis, a rare power even in the Administration, effectively brings down enemies that manage to approach her through the barrages of cannonballs.

Originally, she wanted to become an air-traffic controller, but her tendency to pass out at the sight of blood got in the way and even her appointment as a bridge officer had to be put on hold. At first, she was all but coerced into becoming a field agent by her friend, Lee Sooyeon, but soon realized she was talented in commanding troops and organizing operations.
She became the leader of the artillery division, Maze, at a surprisingly young age, and her preference for safe artillery combat over melee fray has gained support in and out of her troops.
Her only known weakness is that she's all thumbs when it comes to crafting. There are multiple instances in which her handmade accessories terrorized the children who received them.]]
L5_1[1] = L6_1
L5_1[2] = L7_1
L6_1 = {}
L7_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ADMIN_GREATSWORD"
L8_1 = [[
 (This text was restored by a Class 1 Administrator.)
Alex, the deputy commander of the Maze Division, is a vanguard who wields a plasma cannon that has been remodeled into a greatsword. She uses her ability to control waves to attack surrounding enemies, and her power grows stronger the more desperate she becomes.

Originally, one of the clones created by an enemy of the Administration, she was abandoned by her creator for being a failure, and later rescued by the Administration. She was first assigned to the Maze Division which specialized in long-range bombardment operations, because she wasn't strong enough to handle physical combat, but after she mastered how to control her weapon's output, she became a force to be reckoned with.
Many times her ability to carry out field duties were questioned, but her commander's unswayable faith in her and the Division's needs in emergency melee support has kept her in the Division.
The last bastion for her division, she's highly respected among her peers.]]
L6_1[1] = L7_1
L6_1[2] = L8_1
L7_1 = {}
L8_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ADMIN_LEE_SUYEON"
L9_1 = [[
 (This text was restored by Class 1 Administrator.)
Lee Sooyeon is a vanguard who breaks enemy lines with her high HP and area suppression skills.

As a division member, she blindly follows after her master, Hilde. She even pushed herself over the limit to learn difficult skills to satisfy Hilde. The skill was originally named Atomic Hilde Punishment. But it was changed to the current name because Hilde hysterically refused it.
Although her skills are unmatched, she considers charging into the middle of enemies the same as being deployed. Thus, she requires constant guidance and supervision. The commander commented that it is best to let her be. ]]
L7_1[1] = L8_1
L7_1[2] = L9_1
L8_1 = {}
L9_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ADMIN_NA_YUBIN"
L10_1 = [[
 (This text was restored by Class 1 Administrator.)
Na Yubin is an attacker who is responsible for rear fire support for Fenrir Division. He usually carries out control missions, but he launches powerful area attacks in battle to turn the tide.

He is one of the few agents who can assess a situation from a wide perspective. Because he always moves with the post-combat situation in mind, he often gets scolded by other division members for letting his mind wander.
Although Na Yubin has been offered a commander training course by several units he worked with, he keeps refusing the offer for the reason that he still has a lot to learn from Fenrir Division. In response to this, the commander commented that he should first deviate from textbook methodology. ]]
L8_1[1] = L9_1
L8_1[2] = L10_1
L9_1 = {}
L10_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ALPHA_CHOI"
L11_1 = [[
 Gabriel Jun the Vicious Breaker is a powerful guard who enhances allies' evasion with his unique stationary swordsmanship.

He traveled the world and learned various swordsmanship skills, but none of them satisfied him. So he created a new one for himself just in a month. His Stationary Swordsmanship allows him to fend off enemies from all sides, but he is the only person who has been able to master it.
Currently, he is acting as the Judicator of Evil in order to maintain the balance of the world, which he realized while creating his swordsmanship.
* This particular statement is not confirmed to be true. It is just a personal claim of the subject. ]]
L9_1[1] = L10_1
L9_1[2] = L11_1
L10_1 = {}
L11_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ALPHA_CHOWON"
L12_1 = [[
 Kim Chowon is a sniper of Alphatrix Innovation who can quickly reuse the functions installed in her weapon.

She is a veteran mercenary who learned to hunt C.O. before she learned arithmetic. She has spent more than half of her life inside the Counterside while helping the mining of unauthorized groups outside the social boundary. Perhaps because she's had a rough life, she never objects to any absurd operation plans that the leader comes up with.
She is currently attending school to help improve the corporate image, but she is having a difficult time fitting into normal teenage life. Above all, everyone is too polite to her ever since she barehandedly subdued a Counter criminal who broke into the school and went on the rampage. ]]
L10_1[1] = L11_1
L10_1[2] = L12_1
L11_1 = {}
L12_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ALPHA_JIA"
L13_1 = [[
 Shin Jia, the leader of Alphatrix Innovation, is an attacker who fights alongside the realistic illusions she summons.

As the granddaughter of the Alphatrix Group's CEO, she revealed her genius at a young age. But as time passed, her ability to easily complete any tasks in any field earned her avoidance instead of praise. Unfortunately, her talent was not effective when it came to socializing with people.
She was forced to enter the TASKFORCE industry during the feud over the company that occurred after her grandfather's death. Jia's siblings must have wanted her to die in the Counterside, but unfortunately for them, she is still demonstrating her brilliance in fighting against the Corrupted Objects. ]]
L11_1[1] = L12_1
L11_1[2] = L13_1
L12_1 = {}
L13_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ALPHA_LEEJIN"
L14_1 = [[
 Lee Jin is a supporter who burns the enemies in the rear who consider themselves to be safe.

Her flames violently engulf the enemies, but boost the morale of the allies. Lee Jin was the secretary of Alphatrix Group's CEO, and was expected to take a key post in the future. But unfortunately, she was blamed for being a Counter during the feud over the company's ownership, and was demoted to the newly formed promotion team.
Amongst a group of troublemakers and oddballs, Lee Jin has renewed her mind and is trying her best to become a perfect aide for her leader. ]]
L12_1[1] = L13_1
L12_1[2] = L14_1
L13_1 = {}
L14_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ALPHA_SEAROM"
L15_1 = [[
 Oh Saerom is a big fan of the television show, The Masked Counter. She is a vanguard who excels at taking the initiative and speeding up the fight.

Her dream is to become a Counter who defeats evil villains like the Masked Counters. She applied for Alphatrix Innovation despite her family's disapproval, hoping to find fellow heroes who can fight alongside her. Of course, in real life, villains don't appear at the right timing like in the superhero shows. So for now, Saerom is just fighting off Corrupted Objects that threatening civilians. ]]
L13_1[1] = L14_1
L13_1[2] = L15_1
L14_1 = {}
L15_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ALT_KIM_SOBIN"
L16_1 = [[
 Kim Sobin, who is in charge of fire support, is very slow in motion but can deliver massive firepower once she gets into position.

This is because she has the ability to create a dimensional pocket in which she carries an arsenal big enough to fit in a heavy military transporter.
Although she uses various heavy firearms, she doesn't like to see blood. She always prepares bandages and antiseptics in her subspace, so that she can provide first aid to any wounded people she meets, strangers or not.
It is uncertain why someone like her, far from a mercenary, came to the Underground. It is assumed that she was dragged into her position due to her close relations with fellow squad members. ]]
L14_1[1] = L15_1
L14_1[2] = L16_1
L15_1 = {}
L16_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ALT_SEO_YOON"
L17_1 = [[
 Seo Yoon is an attacker who can enhance allies offensive capabilities through outstanding command skills.

She is the commander of ALT Squad who has been performing well in the Underground. The Underground collectively refers to private military organizations that illegally carry out TASKFORCE missions. Among them, betrayals and deceit are a daily occurrence. In such a ruthless environment, she had led her team to complete more than 10 missions within a matter of months without losing a single member.
She refused to open up about her past, but her tactical knowledge shows that she received a professional training similar to that of a military academy. ]]
L15_1[1] = L16_1
L15_1[2] = L17_1
L16_1 = {}
L17_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ALT_XIAOLIN"
L18_1 = [[
 As the youngest in her squad, Xiao Lin makes up for her small physique by mastering her position as a sniper. Her ability to control bioelectricity allows her to make precise shots no matter how fast the target is moving.

During an operation, she excels at the role of scouting enemy activities and collecting information. Her efforts are believed to have greatly contributed to ALT Squad's high mission success rate.
She mainly uses an anti-material sniper rifle, to which she attaches a different accessory every time she completes a mission. She claims that it helps her improve her operational capabilities, but considering how her rifle has been unnecessarily upgraded several times, it appears to be a secret hobby of hers. ]]
L16_1[1] = L17_1
L16_1[2] = L18_1
L17_1 = {}
L18_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ALT_YOO_JIN"
L19_1 = [[
 Eujin is a vanguard who charges enemy lines while dodging attacks.

Her physical prowess is unmatched amongst the Counters of the same grade, and she prefers to brawl at very close range. She lives to fight and eat, and firmly believes all problems can be solved by fighting.
She is a simple-minded person who thinks Eternium and diamond are both pretty rocks, and has a natural talent for combat. During her first mission in the Underground, she beat down a mercenary group for picking on her and was classified as a hazard.
Still she is called the Mastiff, because she gladly jumps into any battle when given the order by her commander. ]]
L17_1[1] = L18_1
L17_1[2] = L19_1
L18_1 = {}
L19_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_AMY"
L20_1 = [[
 Amy Strickland is a vanguard who performs ranged area attacks with her special yoyo. As she gets into the rhythm of battle, her yoyo skills become fancier and faster.

As the leader of the Freedom Riders, Amy never turns away from facing danger. This often drags her into all kinds of trouble, but she always encourages others and manages the crises.
She believes that she has become a Counter in order to help others, and always tries to use her powers in the right place. She does things on her own initiative without expecting a reward, which is a rare attitude in the industry these days.]]
L18_1[1] = L19_1
L18_1[2] = L20_1
L19_1 = {}
L20_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_BD_ELIZABETH"
L21_1 = [[
 Elizabeth Pendragon is an attacker who freely roams the battlefield to perform area attacks.

Prydwen is a secret intelligence agency that has been rumored for a long time. The only truth in all the rumors about this organization is that the Chief of Prydwen has always used the name Pendragon throughout the years.
Descended from a reputable family, Elizabeth is the shining example of noblesse oblige, giving up her peaceful life to serve the royal family and the public.
Handling artifacts from the Counterside is not an elegant job, but she gracefully solves all the challenges she faces at work. The only flaw is that she is doing everything out of groundless confidence. Other agents think of this confident lady as a pretty Tea Bomb. ]]
L19_1[1] = L20_1
L19_1[2] = L21_1
L20_1 = {}
L21_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_BD_ROI"
L22_1 = [[
 Roy Burnett is a vanguard who can break down enemy defenses with the hypergravitational force created from his chains.

Hailed from a ruined noble family, he gained fame in the West End for his outdated gangster fashion and perverse attitude. His father's folly forced him to become a rookie agent at Prydwen, but he doesn't seem to like working as a spy.
He resorts to his fists whenever things go wrong, but those who are subject to his anger are limited to criminals who harass ordinary citizens or bullies who do whatever as they please.
There is an unbelievable rumor that he is actually a model citizen who waits for a green light at a crosswalk even when there is no car on the road. ]]
L20_1[1] = L21_1
L20_1[2] = L22_1
L21_1 = {}
L22_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_BD_RYAN"
L23_1 = [[
 Ryan is a defender who constantly switches his position to parry attacks directed towards him while demolishing the enemy with his iron fists.

As a former soldier of the special forces, he demanded to replace the agency's outdated facility and equipment on his first day at Prydwen. Ever since, he is called the Butler. Living up to his nickname, he always offers guidance, in a polite manner, to the agents who are slacking in their jobs.
Upon facing his iron fists that can can devastate even a C.O. in a single blow, many agents have learned to stay vigilant. But the Chief, along with other Counters, always brings new troubles and tests his iron will. ]]
L21_1[1] = L22_1
L21_1[2] = L23_1
L22_1 = {}
L23_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_BD_THADDEUS"
L24_1 = [[
 Thaddeus Morgan is an attacker who excels at ambushing the enemy's backline.

As the time advances, the value of information grows exponentially. Especially for organizations like Prydwen, which is tracking artifacts in unknown locations. As a former spy who served his nation, Thaddeus Morgan now presents his skills at his new position in Prydwen.
His moves are so well hidden that even the leading intelligence agencies considered him dead until he appeared in public recently. No one knows why he publicly revealed his survival, but everyone who has worked with Thaddeus assumes that he wants to teach a lesson to his previous enemies who've come to get back at him. ]]
L22_1[1] = L23_1
L22_1[2] = L24_1
L23_1 = {}
L24_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_CIVIL_CATHY"
L25_1 = [[
 Cathy Wade is an attacker who performs area attacks by manipulating the local atmosphere.

She used to be a journalist writing sensational articles at a tabloid. While searching for a news item, she exposed the cozy relationship between politicians and a radical environmental group. But she was then targeted by a certain organization which was offended by her article.
She is currently under the protection of the Administration to avoid the constant threats. She seems to be keeping a low profile while helping out her inexperienced commander, but recent investigation revealed that many of the featured articles from Task Planet were actually written by her. ]]
L23_1[1] = L24_1
L23_1[2] = L25_1
L24_1 = {}
L25_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_CIVIL_IRIE"
L26_1 = [[
 Irie Alford joined Official Support because she was looking for something fun.

She is a defender who stops the enemy approach by constantly pushing and knocking them down. Irie's typical day begins with a prank and ends with a prank. Only she knows whether her next prank will be placing a banana peel in front of the conference room door, or switching the entire cafeteria menu to ice cream cakes.
But there are two reasons why she still receives good performance reviews. One is because she pulls pranks even on Corrupted Objects, and the other is because she is quiet when she is eating ice cream. ]]
L24_1[1] = L25_1
L24_1[2] = L26_1
L25_1 = {}
L26_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_CIVIL_ZENA"
L27_1 = [[
 Zena Bird is the commander of the Official Support. She is a late-blooming vanguard who makes up for weak basic stats with skills.

She was the class vice-president when she was caught up in a catastrophe during the graduation trip. She acquired her Watch then, to protect her friends. After escaping the crisis, she joined Official Support to help more people with her newly found powers. The reason why she became the commander, despite her lack of experience as a Counter and a leader, is because no one wanted take the responsibility.
Zena is feeling pressure in her position, but she is constantly trying hard to become the person to match her title. ]]
L25_1[1] = L26_1
L25_1[2] = L27_1
L26_1 = {}
L27_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_DAYMINE_GANGSAN"
L28_1 = " Choi Gangsan is a likable guy with a burly physique resulting from his love for sports.\n\nHe is a defender who taunts enemies and protects allies. His shield created from his Watch, obviously influenced by his experience as a riot cop, looks like an ordinary shield.\nBut it is actually stronger than any Eternium alloy. He is a little bit too sensitive, tightening his guard even upon the minor events of daily life—a Chihuahua walking by or a fumigator truck passing—but he is a righteous man who never spares himself when saving lives."
L26_1[1] = L27_1
L26_1[2] = L28_1
L27_1 = {}
L28_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_DAYMINE_HYUNSOO"
L29_1 = [[
 Park Hyunsoo is the leader of Daymine Mining Team 4. He is a vanguard who is skilled at collaborating with fellow attackers.

He used to be a field assistant who was more familiar with a pen than a sword. But he decided to engage in battle himself to survive the recession and frequent restructuring process.
Before becoming a Counter, he once hovered between life and death due to overworking. Because of the experience, he recommends his team members to only work during business hours and takes responsibility for any extra work.
In the past, he worked hard because he loved his work or because he wanted promotion. But now he is holding his position for his subordinates who rely on him.]]
L27_1[1] = L28_1
L27_1[2] = L29_1
L28_1 = {}
L29_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_DAYMINE_SOMI"
L30_1 = [[
 Shim Somi, a passionate new member of Daymine, is a debilitating supporter who disrupts enemy's offensive capabilities.

When she was working at a call center, she always won the Smile of the Month award. Even after entering the TASKFORCE industry, she never loses her bright smile.
Although she makes a lot of mistakes and often gets scolded by her boss, her experience of dealing with terrible customers helps her quickly shake things off and return to work. She has a strong passion for work, but her goal in life is simply to become a proud daughter to her family. ]]
L28_1[1] = L29_1
L28_1[2] = L30_1
L29_1 = {}
L30_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_DELTA_JAKE"
L31_1 = [[
 Jake Walker is a sturdy vanguard who pushes back enemies with rapid use of skills.

Colonel Walker is a trusted field agent even amongst the elite-oriented Delta Seven. He prefers to find and knock down the source of problem instead of taking the time to devise a plan. Colonel Walker's reckless style has always brought in controversy amongst the command.
But the frontline soldiers have great trust for their superior who always takes the lead. His family has participated in many wars and distinguished themselves in countless battles. Colonel Walker's mindset of caring for his men is assumed to be a part of his family tradition. ]]
L29_1[1] = L30_1
L29_1[2] = L31_1
L30_1 = {}
L31_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_DELTA_KING"
L32_1 = [[
 Dominic King Reginald is a defender who fights more fiercely, the more HP he loses.

During the War, Brigadier General Reginald served under Lieutenant General Antonov. This is not well-known, but according to his men, he worked from the shadows to neutralize political traps and attacks directed at his steadfast superior.
Some military historians even believe that Reginald was the reason the Lieutenant General stayed in power for as long as she did; not because of his political acumen, but also because of his ability to fight, which helped him distinguish himself on the battlefield time and again as the Lieutenant General's right-hand man.
He's a soldier through and through, as his militant appearance suggests. A report by the United Forces, however, says that he's so strong in his own convictions that he could pose new problems.]]
L30_1[1] = L31_1
L30_1[2] = L32_1
L31_1 = {}
L32_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_DELTA_KYLE"
L33_1 = [[
 Kyle Wong is a versatile attacker who uses his gear to scatter enemy attacks while inflicting powerful damage over time.

As a member of Delta Seven's internal investigation team, he is considered as the best example of the federal government's Counter training project. Based on the latest Counter-adapted training he received, he utilizes various Counter gear to maximize the efficiency in battle.
He respects his boss, Lt. General Antonov, and he strives to become a thorough aide worthy of staying by her side. Delta Seven members fear him because he randomly patrols around on a per-second schedule to detect their misbehavior. ]]
L31_1[1] = L32_1
L31_1[2] = L33_1
L32_1 = {}
L33_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_DELTA_MARIA"
L34_1 = [[
 Maria Antonov is an offensive guard who immediately deploys her units to battle while amplifying ally's offensive capabilities.

Lt. General Antonov is a well-known hero who led the Grand Purification War to victory. Her Counter-Corruption doctrine is still used as a standard protocol amongst the TASKFORCE industry.
As a 3rd generation Russian refugee, she is a woman of principle who has reached her current rank with pure abilities despite her superiors' efforts to hold her back. Some say that she continues to personally command unofficial operations throughout the world even after becoming a general.]]
L32_1[1] = L33_1
L32_1[2] = L34_1
L33_1 = {}
L34_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_DELTA_SYLVIA"
L35_1 = [[
 Sylvia Lena Cooper is a sniper who can enhance allied armored units while performing area attacks.

In elementary school, she was already infamous for hacking into the database of her home country's intelligence agency. Of course, she was eventually caught. Instead of spending a life time in a prison, she accepted the offer from Lt. General Antonov.
She is now working at Delta Seven as a civilian electronic warfare consultant. She has no choice but to work with stiff military personnel, but thrilling secret operations seem to fit her well. So far, she has been well-behaved throughout her assigned field work. ]]
L33_1[1] = L34_1
L33_1[2] = L35_1
L34_1 = {}
L35_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_FALLEN_YUMA"
L36_1 = [[
 Frederick Yuma is vanguard who charges enemy lines and engages in a scuffle.

When she's at the detective agency, she can barely calculate the price of the food she ordered, but once she enters battle, she becomes more fearless and aggressive than anyone else.
Yuma doesn't care if her enemy's strong or weak. Gangs in the slum, whom she hangs around, teach their new members to lower their heads as soon as they see Yuma, so she can't pick a fight with them.
To others like them, she's as dangerous as a ticking time bomb, but around her kind brother, Doma, she acts like a puppy who's eager to please.]]
L34_1[1] = L35_1
L34_1[2] = L36_1
L35_1 = {}
L36_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_FREEDOM_KASUMI"
L37_1 = [[
 A defender who draws attention by performing area attacks.

It is a widely accepted theory that a Watch appears to those who develop a strong will to live before death, or to those with an equivalent tenacity. That explains how Hirose Aki could become a Counter. Her obsession towards living an idle life is unmatched.
Aki's ultimate goal is to find a stable source of income. The fastest way to make money would be to become a mercenary, but she has never even imagined herself working.
An experiment proved that Hirose Aki's greatsword changes weight based on the will of its master.]]
L35_1[1] = L36_1
L35_1[2] = L37_1
L36_1 = {}
L37_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_FREEDOM_LEE_MINSEO"
L38_1 = [[
 Lee Minseo is a supporter who hinders enemy movements with ranged area attacks.

She was caught up in a Corruption while ignoring the warnings trying to set a new record in a game, but she miraculously survived by becoming a Counter. The problem is that she only uses her powers for cosplay.
As an avid fan of Necronomiko series, a retro game, Minseo always wears the outfit of the main character from that game. But unlike Necronomiko, who fights bravely against monsters, she is afraid of even fighting a Category 1 C.O., which prevents her from becoming a mercenary.]]
L36_1[1] = L37_1
L36_1[2] = L38_1
L37_1 = {}
L38_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_FREEDOM_LIN"
L39_1 = " An attacker who increases ally reinforcement speed with mysterious powers.\n\nThe cash she sprays around in battle that apparently has her own face printed on it. As someone who pretends to be a lone wolf, Lin Xien is far from being a mercenary. In fact, she is the only daughter of a financial titan.\nShe is running away from home, because she wants to become the greatest gunman like in noir films. Her aides have left a comment for whoever finds her to take care of her, because she will run again if she is sent back home.\nLin Xien's specialty in battle is saying her catch phrase—Leave this to me—and then falling down before returning later without a scar. It is truly an amazing survival skill, but she refuses to explain how it's done because she thinks it's not cool."
L37_1[1] = L38_1
L37_1[2] = L39_1
L38_1 = {}
L39_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_FRONTIER_LEE"
L40_1 = [[
 Lee Dafoe is a defender with excellent skills against multiple enemies. His right arm, covered by steel armor, was created from his Watch. He uses it as shield and weapon.

Lee was once an aspiring boxer, but he lost his right arm when he was jumped by gangsters. He awakened his powers as a Counter after the incident.
Although he lost his dream of becoming a boxer, he is now working at the Frontier with a new goal. Lee is planning to build a hospital back home so that there will be no more victims like him. It doesn't matter that the Frontier is still a small-sized mercenary group. He dreamed of becoming a boxer even in a dark, moldy gym. Now that he has a new arm, he can do anything. ]]
L38_1[1] = L39_1
L38_1[2] = L40_1
L39_1 = {}
L40_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_HB_BOMI"
L41_1 = [[
 As the vanguard of HRT Berry, Bomi humiliates her enemies with her taunting illusions.

Until a few years ago, Bomi used to be a member of a girl group produced by a large entertainment company. But she was asked to leave when doubts were raised on the group's exploitation, because Bomi kept falling asleep whenever she was not dancing.
She wants to show off her new dance moves she made in her dreams, but ever since Miya streamed Bomi talking in her sleep, her sleep streams are more popular than her dance streams. According to the NetTube statistics, 83% of the donations received by HRT Berry comes from Bomi's sleep streams. ]]
L39_1[1] = L40_1
L39_1[2] = L41_1
L40_1 = {}
L41_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_HB_GAEUN"
L42_1 = " Gaeun is an attacker who devastates multiple enemies with chain attacks.\n\nGaeun, the leader of HRT Berry, was born in a country where a civil war had been in progress for two decades. When she was getting used to a life of risking it all just for a piece of bread, she received help from an unknown savior— Teacher—and came out into the world.\nHer only wish is to meet her Teacher again. The reason why she joined HRT Berry without even having a clue about streaming was because Choi Ina convinced her that her Teacher might recognize her if she became famous.\nShe threw other members in panic by not saying a single word during their first stream, but Choi Ina advised her to smile to the camera while thinking of her Teacher. Her bright smile caused thousands of fans to fall for her. "
L40_1[1] = L41_1
L40_1[2] = L42_1
L41_1 = {}
L42_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_HB_MIYA"
L43_1 = [[
 Miya is a sniper who overachieves by gaining morale as she continues to attack. As the cameraperson and editor, she always catches the best moments of her teammates.

She used to be very shy, and stayed at home, indulging in video editing. But ever since she unexpectedly showed up on TV, she started streaming on NetTube for the few fans she acquired.
She is terrible at both playing games and sniping, but she has many stable fans because she is always live except when she's asleep. At first, she was called Mi-Whale for her large figure, but to the delight of her fans, she rapidly lost weight due to her rigorous streaming schedule.
She is still criticized for her lame jokes during opening remarks, and the self-composed song used as the closing theme, but she insists on keeping them. ]]
L41_1[1] = L42_1
L41_1[2] = L43_1
L42_1 = {}
L43_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_HB_RUMI"
L44_1 = [[
 Lumi, who calls herself the next leader of HRT Berry, is a siege unit who quickly breaks through enemy lines to attack the key target. 

Born from a middle-class family, she dreamed of becoming a celebrity ever since she was a kid. But there was always someone better than her regardless of the field.
Tired of being treated second best, she joined HRT Berry as soon as she became a Counter. Of course, her dream of becoming the best was thwarted when Gaeun joined the team.
She will gladly jump into hordes of C.O. if she can draw the attention of the viewers, especially when the enemy leader is spotted. ]]
L42_1[1] = L43_1
L42_1[2] = L44_1
L43_1 = {}
L44_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_HILDE"
L45_1 = [[
 As a vanguard, Hilde engages in close quarters combat at the frontline with powerful area attacks to turn the tide of the battle.

She has been leading the Fenrir Squad since the early days of the Coffin Company, and took down the Category 4 C.O., KRAKEN, to earn the company its official license.
Within the industry, she is notorious for her reckless commands, tackling all problems head on. She took an extended leave of absence for several years, and her whereabouts were unknown until she returned to the scene recently.
During her prime, the excellent individual skills of her squad members were enough to propel the company forward. But now that most of her former colleagues have left, it is yet to be seen whether her recklessness will continue to serve effectively. ]]
L43_1[1] = L44_1
L43_1[2] = L45_1
L44_1 = {}
L45_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_JOO_SHI_YOON"
L46_1 = [[
 A tricky attacker who can counter enemy attacks from anywhere in the battlefield.

His main weapon is the long blade he wears, but he mostly uses only daggers with the excuse that the blade can break his pinky fingernail.
He always claims that he's an ordinary employee, but no one actually believes it. He is the only member who stayed in Fenrir Squad after Hilde disappeared. Many people in the company assume that he only retained his position to keep getting his salary without working.
The leaders of the 52-minute Week Movement and the maintenance team's Drunk-on-duty Incident claim that they had spoken to him before their actions. The Managerial Department is suspecting that he instigated the protests because he wanted to create justifiable reasons to slack off. ]]
L44_1[1] = L45_1
L44_1[2] = L46_1
L45_1 = {}
L46_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_JOO_SHI_YOON_AP"
L47_1 = [[
 Joo Shiyoung is a tricky vanguard specializing in countering her enemies' Normal attacks. She can also improve her Evasion, so she can take on multiple enemies at the same time.

A freelancing mercenary whose motto is "I do as much as I'm paid for," she claims that she's the epitome of professionalism.
An excellent fighter, she keeps a clear dividing line between work and play, and never gets involved in unnecessary fights. Because of this, Delta Seven has assigned her to its detached force, the Pathfinder, under the command of the most rational member it has, for special management.
She becomes helplessly sentimental when she encounters things from her past, which always earns her a lecture from her leader who puts work before everything else. ]]
L45_1[1] = L46_1
L45_1[2] = L47_1
L46_1 = {}
L47_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_KIM_CHEOLSU"
L48_1 = [[
 Kim Chulsoo is a defender who breaks enemy lines with his powerful martial arts.

An ordinary office worker in the past, he survived a sudden Corruption Disaster by dramatically awakening his power as a Counter. His incredible kicks that knocked down C.O. were filmed and went viral. It is said that he unconsciously copied the techniques from a video game he played in his childhood.
He was revered as a hero on the media, but he suffered from the trauma of the catastrophe for a while. Fortunately, he completed the rehabilitation process and decided to return to work. Instead of going back to a normal office, he applied to a TASKFORCE company to fight against C.O.]]
L46_1[1] = L47_1
L46_1[2] = L48_1
L47_1 = {}
L48_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_KYLE_AP"
L49_1 = [[
 Karin Wong is an all-around sniper who uses a special firearm designed for long-range interception to effectively attack enemies in the air and on the ground.

A member of Delta Seven's Internal Investigation Department, she was one of the last members to join the incomplete Counter training project. She passed the experimental training program that developed her analytical ability as Counter with flying colors, proving her capability to handle the special prototype firearm that she uses.
She claims to be the most promising member of Delta Seven and has succeeded on numerous difficult operations. The facial expression of her colleague who was there for a job interview along with her, however, refuted her claim.
She's so obsessed with new technology that she spares no expense in getting all the latest gadgets that she sees.]]
L47_1[1] = L48_1
L47_1[2] = L49_1
L48_1 = {}
L49_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_ORCA"
L50_1 = [[
 Orca is a vanguard who continues her fight by healing off of defeated enemies.

Orca actually refers to the red Watch that shines ominously. According to rumors, Counters who acquire Orca are forced to wander Corrupted Areas and hunt down Corrupted Objects until they die. Some say that the hatred of previous owners infused in Orca forces the new owner to become obsessed with hunting.
Reports of those witnessing Orca owners have never stopped since the Administration was established. Surprisingly, the most recent owner has been reported to be able to partially control the urge to hunt, unlike in previous cases. ]]
L48_1[1] = L49_1
L48_1[2] = L50_1
L49_1 = {}
L50_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_POLICE_LEE_YUMI"
L51_1 = [[
 Lee Yumi is a defender of SWAT 4 who roams the frontline with her excellent evading skills.

Although she is a police officer, she so hostile towards criminals that she often swings her sword instead of handcuffing them. Her behavior has been repeatedly criticized by the mass media, but as the sole Counter within the police force with the highest arrest rate, she remains untouchable even to her superiors.
Her colleague, Kang Soyoung, also knows this and often tries to shift her responsibilities to Yumi. The two always quarrel with each other, but in the face of crime, they become the greatest partners in arms.
Because Yumi is always busy running to the crime scenes, all the bakery owners in the area know her face.]]
L49_1[1] = L50_1
L49_1[2] = L51_1
L50_1 = {}
L51_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_C_SCHOOL_CHAIR"
L52_1 = [[
 The security chair, J.O.U.R., is a long-ranged guard that ensures its rider's uninterrupted sleep. If it receives a certain amount of damage and Edith Twins wakes up, it rises into the air and becomes very aggressive.

Edith Twins, the designer of J.O.U.R., is a member of the Academy Student Council, and has recently been recruited by Future-at-War as an honorary senior researcher. The girl who used to turn house furniture into gadgets she saw in sci-fi movies and animation has grown into a genius engineering scientist.
But when others' expectations of her interfered with her favorite pastime, napping, she finally accepted the Academy's admission offer and left behind her lab life to start living as a Grade D Counter student.
Even now, she designs transformative robots for Future-at-War as a hobby, but no one know what our life could have been if she gave up on napping and focused on research.]]
L50_1[1] = L51_1
L50_1[2] = L52_1
