L20_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_SOF_JANE"
L21_1 = [[
 Jane Doe is a vanguard with high evasion who stays in battle while performing area attacks.

Jane Doe usually refers to an anonymous woman, but it is also a false name used by this woman. Nothing is known about this mercenary, including her name, age, and background. Even on the verge of death, she hides her thoughts behind a smile. The only thing the documents say about her is that she is an excellent killer.
She claims to be a member of the Mason Mercenary Office, but it seems like she is borrowing the name without permission because John always clenches his teeth whenever he hears her name.]]
L19_1[1] = L20_1
L19_1[2] = L21_1
L20_1 = {}
L21_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_SOF_JOHN"
L22_1 = [[
 An attacker who fights with custom-built drones and enhances allied armored units. 

Surprisingly, John Mason has a doctorate degree in engineering which is unusual for a mercenary. He acquired his degree so quickly that he was even offered a job as professor. He isn't lying when he calls himself an intelligent mercenary.
John roams the battlefield alone, equipped with the cutting edge gear he invented. Probably because he learned from an experienced veteran that money often causes conflict among mercenaries, he insists on keeping a one-man office.
However, his office has never made profit ever since its establishment, because he only chooses the most expensive materials to build his own gear. ]]
L20_1[1] = L21_1
L20_1[2] = L22_1
L21_1 = {}
L22_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_STATE_AIRBORNE"
L23_1 = [[
 All-around paratroopers with high attack power that can be deployed anywhere.

They specialize in infiltrating the enemy's rear, cutting off reinforcements and fire support. Although they have dirty mouths, they are always willing to jump into danger.]]
L21_1[1] = L22_1
L21_1[2] = L23_1
L22_1 = {}
L23_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_STATE_ENGINEER"
L24_1 = [[
 A supporter infantry unit that specializes in repairing and enhancing ally mech units.

They manage armored units on site, enabling the costly equipment to stay longer on the frontline. When off duty, they sometime repair company facilities for free.]]
L22_1[1] = L23_1
L22_1[2] = L24_1
L23_1 = {}
L24_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_STATE_RIFLE"
L25_1 = [[
 This attacker periodically performs area attacks, and grows stronger with each attack.

They are the base units of U.S. national defense. They are engaged in an anti-Corruption war, testing the new gear developed in an army innovation project. C.O. will soon fear the Stars and Stripes.]]
L23_1[1] = L24_1
L23_1[2] = L25_1
L24_1 = {}
L25_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_TIDE_GRENADE"
L26_1 = [[
 A snipers who performs area attacks with grenades.

Sweepers are attackers who are deployed to subdue hostile targets who are encamped indoors. Composed of former snipers, they are capable of guaranteeing a hit even when using grenade launchers.
It is often said that they are the most eccentric people in the Black Tide. They always act leisurely, probably because they have confidence in their marksmanship skills. But their love for donuts and sense of duty to protect citizens are no different from others.]]
L24_1[1] = L25_1
L24_1[2] = L26_1
L25_1 = {}
L26_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_TIDE_GUNSHIELD"
L27_1 = [[
 A defender who can launch all-around attacks while moving.

Strongholds are subjugation units deployed to prevent further damage in urban warfare. Their heavy reinforced suits prevent nearly all conventional personal weapons.
They are mostly composed of retired police officers. As the veterans who remained in battlefields from the Administration Failure to the Grand Purification War, they will gladly draw the attention of enemies with a pistol. They prefer to take on enemy attacks themselves rather than to lose a comrade. ]]
L25_1[1] = L26_1
L25_1[2] = L27_1
L26_1 = {}
L27_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_TIDE_SHOTGUN"
L28_1 = [[
 A vanguard who pushes back enemies with area attacks to reduce their defense.

Terminators are special agents who are deployed upon a C.O. appearance. The reinforced Terminator armor is nearly as strong as a human-sized heavy equipment. But their deployment is limited because the armor requires a painful process of welding the circuits directly to the central nerves.
These units are recruited through a strict screening only when police officers who have acquired moderate physical disabilities during their duties express their willingness to volunteer.]]
L26_1[1] = L27_1
L26_1[2] = L28_1
L27_1 = {}
L28_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_TIDE_SUBMACHINEGUN"
L29_1 = [[
 A ranged attacker who grows stronger as the battle goes on.

Scouts are the units initially used in battle, removing enemy threats with a preemptive strike. Armed with lightweight combat suits and submachine guns, they roam through dangerous battlefields to help allies breech enemy lines and acquire valuable information.
Many of them are known to be blabbermouths, but maybe it is the only way for them to relieve the stress and fear they experience in battle. ]]
L27_1[1] = L28_1
L27_1[2] = L29_1
L28_1 = {}
L29_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_S_YG_SORIM"
L30_1 = [[
 Han Sorim is an all-around ranged attacker who attacks faster as she grows familiar to battle.

She is the secondary leader of the animal rescue club, White Rabbit. Although she hates all forms of physical activities, she is a very fast learner. In her first simulation training, she scored well above the averages of soldiers in weapon utilization and shooting, only with the knowledge she learned by watching others.
Sorim always calls Harim Captain, because she has become a military maniac through a variety of media including comic books. She is living under the fantasy that she is a soldier, but she becomes a shy girl again when she gets nervous.
Her future looks bright because she is a genius who gravitates toward what she likes.]]
L28_1[1] = L29_1
L28_1[2] = L30_1
L29_1 = {}
L30_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_ACADEMY_FRESHMAN"
L31_1 = "  The Operator Training Institute sends out its senior students with good grades to affiliated TASKFORCE companies as part of their field training. Most trainees go back to the Institute after their contract period to finish their training, but in some cases, they're offered a place in the company on the spot. Every trainee hopes for the latter and tries her best to impress her employer every day."
L29_1[1] = L30_1
L29_1[2] = L31_1
L30_1 = {}
L31_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_ALICIA"
L32_1 = [[
  Lime is a subsequent version of mass-market software developed by Future-at-War. While the earlier version was mainly focused on practicality, Lime was advertised as an AI secretary that provided unique expressions and interaction functions.
 It may not perform as well as Alphatrix's competing product that was released later, but still in demand thanks to the product's reliability, and a wide selection of add-ons were added over the years. ]]
L30_1[1] = L31_1
L30_1[2] = L32_1
L31_1 = {}
L32_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_ANASTASIA"
L33_1 = [[
  Anastasia is a former assistant to Professor Olivie Park. She changed her major from biology to mechanical engineering halfway through.
 She joined the Coffin Company to work off her debt, a student loan that she took out with the company to get Eternium devices needed for research purposes.
 An Administration-certified Grade D Counter, she uses her Counter ability to move heavy components and perform manual centrifugation because her company can't afford advanced equipment.]]
L31_1[1] = L32_1
L31_1[2] = L33_1
L32_1 = {}
L33_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_AUTOMATA"
L34_1 = [[
  Mass-market Automaton is mass-market software created by Future-at-War to replace human military staff and support the basic operations of dimensional ships.
 Originally military supply software, it's now also available for civil purposes. The earlier version was bare bones with no graphics whatsoever, but after an add-on that provided a girl character received rave reviews, it was officially included in the software.]]
L32_1[1] = L33_1
L32_1[2] = L34_1
L33_1 = {}
L34_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_CHLOE"
L35_1 = [[
  Chloe trained at the Operator Training Institute. She's more passionate about the groundless theories of the occult that she found on the Internet than about her job.
 Claiming to be talented in divination, she spends most of her paychecks on buying crystal balls and other dubious occult paraphernalia. According to other employees who experienced her fortune-telling, her readings, unlike the overall questionable impression, are surprisingly accurate.
 She's classmates with another recruit, Lena Mackenzie, whom she claims to have been trying to enlighten. Those around her said it's actually Lena who keeps Chloe on the straight and narrow.]]
L33_1[1] = L34_1
L33_1[2] = L35_1
L34_1 = {}
L35_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_JANG_WEI"
L36_1 = [[
  Zhang Wei is a talented bookkeeper who always got involved with the wrong people until she settled down at John Mason's Mercenary Office.
 She spends most of her time at the office touching up her makeup or browsing the Internet. Her boss thinks she's lazy, but given her track record, the less work she has to do, the more transparent the company's finances. To her, working hard means a lot of money laundering.]]
L34_1[1] = L35_1
L34_1[2] = L36_1
L35_1 = {}
L36_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_KIMHANA"
L37_1 = [[
  Manager Kim Hana is an essential member of the Coffin Company who leads the others by example and kindness.
 She joined the company right after she graduated from high school. Her cheerful smile brightens up the office atmosphere that sometimes borders on being drab.
 Personally, however, she's having a hard time finding the right man. She went on numerous blind dates, but none of them led to a second date. Her colleagues suspect that might have something to do with her being a terrible drunk.  ]]
L35_1[1] = L36_1
L35_1[2] = L37_1
L36_1 = {}
L37_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_LEE_SUYEON"
L38_1 = [[
  Lee Sooyeon is the founder of the Coffin Company. When the new CEO appeared, she stepped down to become vice president.
 The Coffin Company was once known as a sweatshop. When it started growing rapidly, however, its surprisingly high non-accident rate gained attention. Lee Sooyeon was nominated as one of the main contributing factors, being someone who knows how to manage as well as operate in the field. Personally, she always complains that she feels as if she's carrying a ticking time bomb, thanks to employees who won't stop causing trouble.]]
L36_1[1] = L37_1
L36_1[2] = L38_1
L37_1 = {}
L38_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_LEE_YOONJUNG"
L39_1 = [[
  Lee Yoonjung, the assistant to Dr. Olivie Park, lives on caffeine to keep herself awake while helping her boss with her theses.
 Her caffeine intake is so dangerously high that it would have crippled most people. So far, she hasn't had any debilitating health problems, thanks to her genetics. But she can't hide the dark circles under her eyes or the gloomy, depressing aura around her.
 It's hard to believe she used to be cheerful and popular back in her university days.]]
L37_1[1] = L38_1
L37_1[2] = L39_1
L38_1 = {}
L39_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_MARK_FINRI"
L40_1 = [[
 Mark Finley is an intelligence agent who's been on spy missions everywhere in the world since he his youth. He was especially highly praised by his superiors for his ability to carry out operations on the dangerous Counterside.
 Currently, he's believed to be part of the Administration Coalition Command Intelligence Office. Considering his career, however, this may also be a disguise.]]
L38_1[1] = L39_1
L38_1[2] = L40_1
L39_1 = {}
L40_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_MASTER"
L41_1 = [[
  The Mansion Master is the leader of the assassin group, Mansion, and she's being pursued by the Administration Coalition Command Intelligence Office under suspicion of manufacturing and distributing lethal poisons.
 Knowledgeable in botany, this noble lady uses plant-derived toxins to make her Maids fearless or paralyze her enemies' senses. It's impossible to know how many victims of her poisons have been brushed off as natural deaths.
 The garden in her mansion is unbelievably gorgeous, but it's better not to even imagine what might be buried under those beautifully blooming flowers.]]
L39_1[1] = L40_1
L39_1[2] = L41_1
L40_1 = {}
L41_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_NAHIRIN"
L42_1 = "  Na Heerin is a dimensional ship enthusiast who joined the industry to become like her father, one of the earliest dimensional ship designers. For now, she's taking care of minuscule administrative tasks at the hangar of a small TASKFORCE company, but she's not complaining. At least she can see dimensional ships up close as they take off. She dreams of one day building the surrealistic dimensional ship that she herself designed."
L40_1[1] = L41_1
L40_1[2] = L42_1
L41_1 = {}
L42_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_OLD_ALICIA"
L43_1 = "Moneka is a Division support control system extracted from an Old Administration's ship salvaged from the Counterside. This model, always showing the highest level of emotional expression, has been used not only for tactical support, but also for armored weapons. After a complete restoration, Moneka is now fully prepared for a rapid advance. Behind her soft smile lies a fatal charm."
L41_1[1] = L42_1
L41_1[2] = L43_1
L42_1 = {}
L43_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_OLIVIA_PARK"
L44_1 = [[
  Olivie Park is an authority in Counter research and Corruption biology, with numerous theses under her belt that surprised the academic world with their brilliance every time they were released. She was instrumental in elevating the new field of study, Corruption biology, to its current level.
 Not many people know that behind her remarkable academic achievements exist a ruthless experimental spirit and countless assistants' sacrifices.]]
L42_1[1] = L43_1
L42_1[2] = L44_1
L43_1 = {}
L44_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_RAS_TOWER"
L45_1 = [[
  Sigma is the head of the Future Strategy Department and an exemplary employee who never deviates from her daily tasks: reading storybooks, letting her imagination run wild, and responding to her daddy's calls.
 But it's when she works as an Operator that Sigma truly shines. She's the world's most excellent unlicensed pilot, with an accident rate of zero, capable of one-dimensional strategies that even elementary students can understand. So, don't be surprised if you hear a little girl barking orders at the rest of the ship's staff.]]
L43_1[1] = L44_1
L43_1[2] = L45_1
L44_1 = {}
L45_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_REPLACER_COMMANDAR"
L46_1 = "  The supporters of the Replacer Syndicate's twisted ideals include ex-military officers. They use the knowledge and experience gained during their military days to train others systematically and strategically, contributing to their organization's growth into becoming a veritable threat to the rest of the world. Some of them surrendered during battle, but most still believe that they're the chosen people."
L44_1[1] = L45_1
L44_1[2] = L46_1
L45_1 = {}
L46_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_OPR_REPLACER_KING"
L47_1 = [[
  The Replacer King is the founder of the Replacer Syndicate. He's suggested to his researchers various ways of using the Replacer Factor. One of them is to use it and militantly contain various problems that he might encounter while carrying out his plans.
 His military doctrines based on Replacer Hybriders have spread quickly through the ex-military officers in his organization, but it's doubtful that any one of them can put them to use as well as their originator, the Replacer King, can.]]
L45_1[1] = L46_1
L45_1[2] = L47_1
L46_1 = {}
L47_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_REAPER_M_RAILGUN"
L48_1 = [[
Grendel is a sniper that deals powerful damage to enemies protected by a barrier.
The [Hammer of Justice], developed by the Ordnance Development Agency of the Northern Union, was a railgun installed in the mountain area to destroy the defensive force fields generated by some Corrupted Objects. However, the Northern Union desired to use this massive firepower for more diverse purposes, which resulted in Grendel.
The crude, multi-limbed mobile weapon was designed as an operational platform for the Hammer of Justice. After the limitations of its power usage were overcome through the use of energy cylinders, Grendel has excelled in her role as a sentinel protecting the border.]]
L46_1[1] = L47_1
L46_1[2] = L48_1
