L19_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_ADMIN_CA_BIRDCAGE"
L20_1 = [[
Solovey is a Counter who can promote plant growth using CRF.
Based on her will, the plants can change their shape or size, as well as sprout thorns or bloom flowers. Her equivalent of a Watch is a birdcage, inside which a blooming flower reflects her CRF status. She also possesses another Watch, though it appears to be nonfunctional at the moment. 
She has no experience with social activities and lacks basic common sense, requiring considerable attention and guidance. Although she frequently expresses her desire to become an adult quickly, she also loves dolls and animated cartoons, often showing a struggle within herself. 
Drawing is her hobby; she once drew a portrait of her counselor, but it is evident that she needs much more practice.]]
L18_1[1] = L19_1
L18_1[2] = L20_1
L19_1 = {}
L20_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_ALT_C_SEO_YOON_PR"
L21_1 = [[
The leader of the ALT Squad, a recently licensed as an official TASKFORCE by the Administration.
While her CRF output is average, she has a high understanding of her own abilities and excels at applying them effectively. In addition to her Counter ability, she is skilled in reading people and steering them as intended, showcasing excellent interpersonal tactics. Although she usually uses these skills for personal gain, she demonstrates remarkable loyalty and dedication once trust is established, which sets her apart from people with typical individualistic tendencies. 
Following an injury, she claims to be using lighter weapons as part of her rehabilitation. However, it has been confirmed that her CRF output and individual capabilities show no significant abnormalities.]]
L19_1[1] = L20_1
L19_1[2] = L21_1
L20_1 = {}
L21_1 = "SI_COLLECTION_UNIT_INTRO_NKM_UNIT_CORRUPTED_C_MIMIC"
L22_1 = [[
The subject has been identified as an Irregular that reacts to the CRF of Counters, unlike typical C.O.s. She is a Hive-Mind C.O. formed by the gathering of multiple viruses.
While she takes on a human form during activity, she appears to use clothing to hide organs presumed to store Corruption energy (suspected to be horns and a tail).
The subject shows interest in observing human behavior and attempts to understand its principles, suggesting high intelligence. She is particularly curious about the concepts of crime, and good and evil. However, her instinct to absorb CRF seems to override any consideration of the target's good or evil nature.
If time and budget allow, experiments will be conducted to determine the possibility of coexistence with humans.
The above content is an excerpt from Dr. Lone Lee's research report.]]
L20_1[1] = L21_1
L20_1[2] = L22_1
L21_1 = {}
